1
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:17,800
Hello?

2
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:19,350
Qin, can you hear me?

3
00:00:19,710 --> 00:00:20,710
The suspect has a gun!

4
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:21,920
Qin!

5
00:00:23,230 --> 00:00:24,120
Darn walkie-talkie.

6
00:00:30,580 --> 00:00:31,460
(Police)

7
00:00:39,320 --> 00:00:40,150
Dad.

8
00:00:41,960 --> 00:00:42,750
Dad.

9
00:00:47,520 --> 00:00:48,320
Captain Qin.

10
00:00:49,960 --> 00:00:51,640
Xiaoshan, hello.

11
00:00:51,710 --> 00:00:53,640
Zhang Daxin hid a gun in a paper box.

12
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:54,560
Who told you that?

13
00:00:54,560 --> 00:00:56,110
Zhou called and told me.

14
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:58,560
He said your son, Ming, told him.

15
00:01:00,030 --> 00:01:00,840
Got it.

16
00:01:01,070 --> 00:01:01,790
Li,

17
00:01:01,790 --> 00:01:04,070
take Zhang Daxin's son to talk to him.

18
00:01:04,310 --> 00:01:05,640
Try to buy as much time as possible.

19
00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:06,430
Me?

20
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:15,840
Xiaoshan, come with me.

21
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:21,280
Zhang Daxin,

22
00:01:22,430 --> 00:01:23,680
look who's here.

23
00:01:23,840 --> 00:01:25,680
Your son was crying to see you.

24
00:01:27,430 --> 00:01:28,680
Easy, easy.

25
00:01:31,310 --> 00:01:32,120
Xiaoshan.

26
00:01:33,310 --> 00:01:34,870
Why did you bring my son here?

27
00:01:35,070 --> 00:01:35,870
Zhang Daxin,

28
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:37,000
think about it.

29
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:38,120
If something happens to you,

30
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:39,200
what will happen to your son?

31
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:40,680
What will he think of you
when he grows up?

32
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:43,350
Mind your own business!

33
00:01:43,590 --> 00:01:44,400
Son,

34
00:01:45,280 --> 00:01:46,280
come to me.

35
00:01:47,040 --> 00:01:48,120
Dad,

36
00:01:48,760 --> 00:01:50,480
don't do anything wrong.

37
00:01:50,640 --> 00:01:53,430
Let's go home, Dad.

38
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:54,680
Zhang Daxin,

39
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:56,200
you have to trust us.

40
00:01:56,230 --> 00:01:58,070
Trust that the law
will give you justice.

41
00:01:58,200 --> 00:01:59,970
Why did you bring my son here?

42
00:01:59,970 --> 00:02:01,460
- Zhang Daxin, calm down.
- So he could see me like this?

43
00:02:01,460 --> 00:02:03,330
- He insisted on coming to find you.
- What are you up to?

44
00:02:03,330 --> 00:02:04,150
I don't believe you.

45
00:02:04,150 --> 00:02:06,040
I want you all to
pay for my wife's life.

46
00:02:52,870 --> 00:02:53,680
Li.

47
00:02:57,630 --> 00:02:58,430
Stay still.

48
00:03:04,590 --> 00:03:06,470
Your son was crying to see you.

49
00:03:08,730 --> 00:03:10,890
Dad...

50
00:03:11,020 --> 00:03:13,600
Let's go home.

51
00:03:23,910 --> 00:03:25,820
Dad.

52
00:03:25,820 --> 00:03:29,540
=Medical Examiner Dr. Qin: Bones of the Past=
=Episode 14=

53
00:03:29,540 --> 00:03:31,140
(PSB Criminal Investigation Detachment)
Up, down.

54
00:03:31,210 --> 00:03:33,480
Patting hands, one by one...

55
00:03:34,590 --> 00:03:35,430
Dad.

56
00:03:35,610 --> 00:03:36,870
- Dad.
- Son.

57
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:40,360
Why are you here?

58
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:42,400
Ming insisted on coming to find you.

59
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:43,630
I don't know what got into him.

60
00:03:43,840 --> 00:03:45,470
He kept shouting
that you were in danger.

61
00:03:45,470 --> 00:03:46,120
Are you okay?

62
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:47,430
What could happen to me?

63
00:03:47,470 --> 00:03:48,710
My son just missed me,

64
00:03:48,710 --> 00:03:49,360
right?

65
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:50,080
Give me a kiss.

66
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:52,120
Good boy.

67
00:03:52,120 --> 00:03:52,750
Dad,

68
00:03:52,750 --> 00:03:55,710
I finished the task
Mr. Know-It-All gave me.

69
00:03:55,710 --> 00:03:56,870
Aren't I awesome?

70
00:03:57,310 --> 00:03:58,800
You really are awesome.

71
00:03:59,430 --> 00:04:01,280
You saved me once again, didn't you?

72
00:04:27,430 --> 00:04:28,310
Have you eaten yet?

73
00:04:28,310 --> 00:04:28,820
Not yet.

74
00:04:28,820 --> 00:04:30,020
Let's eat at the cafeteria then.

75
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:31,870
He'll be thrilled then.

76
00:04:31,870 --> 00:04:32,600
Right?

77
00:05:33,310 --> 00:05:34,120
Qin?

78
00:05:35,360 --> 00:05:36,680
Why are you sleeping here?

79
00:05:36,770 --> 00:05:37,870
You're pushing yourself way too hard.

80
00:05:37,870 --> 00:05:38,950
Go back and get some rest.

81
00:05:44,950 --> 00:05:45,870
Where is Zhang Xiaoshan?

82
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:47,510
Zhang Xiaoshan?

83
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:49,070
Who is Zhang Xiaoshan?

84
00:05:52,240 --> 00:05:53,480
The hitman hired by Li Yan.

85
00:05:53,870 --> 00:05:55,560
What hitman did Li Yan hire?

86
00:05:57,800 --> 00:05:58,600
Section Chief Qin,

87
00:06:00,310 --> 00:06:01,630
didn't you ask me
to check if Zhang Daxin

88
00:06:01,630 --> 00:06:02,630
had a criminal record?

89
00:06:04,800 --> 00:06:06,160
Back in 1990,

90
00:06:06,160 --> 00:06:08,240
he injured a man named Huo Jianjun.

91
00:06:08,630 --> 00:06:10,240
He was sentenced
to one year in prison for that.

92
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:12,680
If that's the case,

93
00:06:13,070 --> 00:06:14,630
Zhang Daxin didn't kill Qin Tian,

94
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,310
so he wasn't sentenced to death.

95
00:06:16,920 --> 00:06:18,750
So, Zhang Xiaoshan
wouldn't have lost his father

96
00:06:18,750 --> 00:06:19,750
and gone down the wrong path.

97
00:06:19,830 --> 00:06:21,160
Li Yan wouldn't have hired a killer,

98
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:22,560
so Li Yan's fate...

99
00:06:24,430 --> 00:06:25,720
Didn't you say before

100
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:28,070
that Li Yan told you
he always wanted to die?

101
00:06:28,430 --> 00:06:29,360
Let me think...

102
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:45,830
What are you doing?

103
00:06:45,900 --> 00:06:47,260
- You've disappointed me so much.
- Don't think that just because you

104
00:06:47,260 --> 00:06:47,850
got into a third-tier college,

105
00:06:47,850 --> 00:06:49,600
you can come bother my son preparing
for Tsinghua or Peking University.

106
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:50,750
Listen.

107
00:06:50,750 --> 00:06:51,830
You're not worthy.

108
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:52,870
Do you hear me?

109
00:06:56,800 --> 00:06:57,600
Li Yan,

110
00:06:58,600 --> 00:07:00,120
having parents like yours

111
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:02,160
is pathetic.

112
00:07:02,160 --> 00:07:03,920
Hey, how dare you say that!

113
00:07:03,920 --> 00:07:05,040
Get out of here!

114
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:06,600
Get out.

115
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:12,720
What are you doing?

116
00:07:18,190 --> 00:07:19,600
What is wrong with kids these days?

117
00:07:20,430 --> 00:07:21,870
Look at what she did
to your mother's hand.

118
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:30,870
Li Yan, what are you trying to do?

119
00:08:30,870 --> 00:08:31,850
Calm the kid down first.

120
00:08:31,850 --> 00:08:33,580
We can talk about
Tsinghua or Peking University later.

121
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:37,550
(You're never going
to change for me, right?)

122
00:08:41,150 --> 00:08:41,960
Li Yan!

123
00:08:59,860 --> 00:09:02,340
(Longfan City People's Hospital,
Outpatient Building)

124
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:06,440
Thank you, Officer Qin.

125
00:09:06,790 --> 00:09:08,150
You saved Li Yan.

126
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:10,360
As his parents,

127
00:09:10,360 --> 00:09:11,600
we really can't thank you enough.

128
00:09:12,150 --> 00:09:13,000
Thank you so much.

129
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:14,000
There's no need to thank me.

130
00:09:15,790 --> 00:09:16,630
After all, these things...

131
00:09:16,630 --> 00:09:17,440
We were wrong.

132
00:09:17,790 --> 00:09:19,320
We were completely wrong.

133
00:09:19,390 --> 00:09:21,240
We got it all wrong.

134
00:09:22,480 --> 00:09:24,840
I'll never push him to get
into top universities again.

135
00:09:24,840 --> 00:09:26,320
Never again.

136
00:09:26,870 --> 00:09:27,840
How did...

137
00:09:28,150 --> 00:09:29,840
How did it turn out like this?

138
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:33,630
We...

139
00:09:33,840 --> 00:09:36,150
We just wanted to give him the best.

140
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:39,440
We gave him all our love.

141
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:45,120
Yet it was your love

142
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:48,840
that turned into the hands
pushing him toward death.

143
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:49,910
How...

144
00:09:50,320 --> 00:09:53,390
How could we ever want him to die?

145
00:10:00,380 --> 00:10:01,320
You're Li Yan's parents, right?

146
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:01,960
Yes, we are.

147
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:02,730
Alright.

148
00:10:02,750 --> 00:10:03,750
His cast is on now.

149
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,230
He just needs to rest and recover.

150
00:10:05,560 --> 00:10:06,180
Thank you, Doctor.

151
00:10:06,180 --> 00:10:07,510
- You're welcome.
- Thank you so much.

152
00:10:07,910 --> 00:10:08,720
Yan.

153
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:10,200
Yan, are you okay?

154
00:10:10,200 --> 00:10:10,960
Yan...

155
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:15,440
I was wrong.

156
00:10:15,960 --> 00:10:17,510
I will never push you again.

157
00:10:17,510 --> 00:10:18,320
Okay?

158
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:22,000
Didn't you...

159
00:10:22,670 --> 00:10:24,510
Didn't you want
to climb snowy mountains?

160
00:10:24,550 --> 00:10:26,320
I will go with you. I support you.

161
00:10:26,320 --> 00:10:27,670
We'll go together once you get better,

162
00:10:27,670 --> 00:10:28,390
all right?

163
00:10:28,550 --> 00:10:29,360
Son,

164
00:10:30,270 --> 00:10:32,600
from now on, whatever decision you make,

165
00:10:32,910 --> 00:10:34,320
I will support you.

166
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:36,320
I will respect

167
00:10:36,750 --> 00:10:37,750
every choice you make.

168
00:10:38,150 --> 00:10:39,630
As long as you're safe and sound,

169
00:10:39,750 --> 00:10:41,320
nothing else matters more.

170
00:10:42,240 --> 00:10:43,030
Yan...

171
00:11:02,390 --> 00:11:03,790
Officer, are you alright?

172
00:11:03,870 --> 00:11:04,670
I'm fine.

173
00:11:07,390 --> 00:11:08,240
I'm good.

174
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:11,150
Never been better.

175
00:11:45,390 --> 00:11:46,150
Who are you going with?

176
00:11:46,150 --> 00:11:46,960
Let's go, baby.

177
00:11:48,480 --> 00:11:49,390
My good grandson.

178
00:11:50,200 --> 00:11:51,000
Baby,

179
00:11:51,480 --> 00:11:52,960
what do you call my daddy?

180
00:11:53,510 --> 00:11:54,440
Grandpa.

181
00:11:55,150 --> 00:11:56,270
Baby, look at Grandpa.

182
00:11:56,870 --> 00:11:58,030
My big grandson.

183
00:11:58,460 --> 00:11:58,960
Here we go.

184
00:11:58,980 --> 00:12:00,070
Come on, say "Grandpa" for me.

185
00:12:01,630 --> 00:12:02,440
Here we go.

186
00:12:26,060 --> 00:12:28,860
(Zhang Daxin's Fingerprint Impression)

187
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:34,500
(Fingerprint Impression
from Bai Wen's House)

188
00:12:36,870 --> 00:12:39,600
Captain Qin, everything matches.

189
00:12:40,020 --> 00:12:41,120
This fingerprint
was found on a tissue pack

190
00:12:41,120 --> 00:12:42,790
at Bai Wen's house.

191
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:45,670
It's an exact match with Zhang Daxin.

192
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:47,120
And

193
00:12:48,720 --> 00:12:50,320
this is a right forefoot print

194
00:12:50,630 --> 00:12:52,320
found at Bai Wen's house.

195
00:12:53,600 --> 00:12:55,240
The unique triangular wear pattern

196
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:56,440
and the shifted pressure point on it

197
00:12:56,750 --> 00:12:58,200
match Zhang Daxin perfectly.

198
00:12:59,600 --> 00:13:01,510
With so much evidence
pointing to Zhang Daxin,

199
00:13:01,790 --> 00:13:03,840
can we suspect

200
00:13:04,270 --> 00:13:06,910
that the serial killer
responsible for multiple victims

201
00:13:07,480 --> 00:13:08,510
is Zhang Daxin?

202
00:13:09,390 --> 00:13:10,670
Hey, don't be so impulsive.

203
00:13:11,050 --> 00:13:12,530
We'll only know after interrogating him.

204
00:13:13,040 --> 00:13:14,270
Let's go interrogate him.

205
00:13:14,340 --> 00:13:15,270
Move it.

206
00:13:15,450 --> 00:13:16,440
- What are you waiting for?
- Let's interrogate him.

207
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:17,600
Nobody said we wouldn't.

208
00:13:17,960 --> 00:13:18,910
Come on, let's go.

209
00:13:19,790 --> 00:13:20,770
You're quite something, huh?

210
00:13:20,770 --> 00:13:21,840
(Confess for Leniency,
Resist for Severity)

211
00:13:21,840 --> 00:13:23,030
Making your own homemade gun?

212
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:24,630
Talk.

213
00:13:24,720 --> 00:13:27,000
How did you lure Huo Jianjun over
and hold him hostage?

214
00:13:27,150 --> 00:13:29,270
You don't arrest those scammers
at the Urban Construction Group,

215
00:13:29,270 --> 00:13:30,440
yet you arrest me?

216
00:13:31,320 --> 00:13:32,720
I'm a victim too.

217
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:34,000
Those scammers?

218
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:35,870
Which scammers?

219
00:13:36,030 --> 00:13:38,150
Huo Qicheng and Liang Chao.

220
00:13:38,480 --> 00:13:39,390
I know he's dead.

221
00:13:39,390 --> 00:13:40,790
Liang Chao deserved to die.

222
00:13:40,790 --> 00:13:42,480
They deserved to die.

223
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:43,960
Serves them right.

224
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:45,630
How exactly did you do it?

225
00:13:45,750 --> 00:13:47,000
How did I do what?

226
00:13:48,910 --> 00:13:51,390
You don't actually think
I killed Liang Chao, do you?

227
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:55,910
We found your fingerprints
at Bai Wen's house.

228
00:13:56,360 --> 00:13:57,840
And someone is willing to testify

229
00:13:57,840 --> 00:13:59,550
that you said you killed Liang Chao.

230
00:13:59,790 --> 00:14:01,320
Not only did you kill Liang Chao,

231
00:14:01,390 --> 00:14:02,720
but you also killed Huo Qicheng

232
00:14:02,720 --> 00:14:04,870
and slashed Huo Qicheng's brother,
Huo Jianjun.

233
00:14:05,030 --> 00:14:05,840
Is that right?

234
00:14:09,750 --> 00:14:11,390
I didn't kill Liang Chao.

235
00:14:12,510 --> 00:14:14,240
Though I wish I had.

236
00:14:14,960 --> 00:14:16,670
Do you know where you are right now?

237
00:14:17,270 --> 00:14:19,000
Get your head straight!

238
00:14:19,630 --> 00:14:21,720
All the evidence points directly to you,

239
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:23,790
and you're still sitting here
arguing with us?

240
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:26,720
Confess everything
down to the last detail.

241
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:28,870
Speak.

242
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:50,240
Do you know what you're doing?

243
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:52,440
You're using your ignorant stubbornness

244
00:14:52,670 --> 00:14:54,000
to defy the law.

245
00:14:54,870 --> 00:14:55,910
Do you have any idea

246
00:14:58,360 --> 00:15:00,630
what your son is doing
at this very moment?

247
00:15:02,510 --> 00:15:03,960
Our fellow officers

248
00:15:05,390 --> 00:15:06,910
are staying by his side while he sleeps.

249
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:08,870
Tomorrow morning,

250
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:12,030
they'll be taking your son to school.

251
00:15:12,640 --> 00:15:13,720
In the afternoon,

252
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:16,320
they'll pick him up after school.

253
00:15:18,550 --> 00:15:20,000
Without them,

254
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:22,200
what would happen to your son?

255
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:24,080
If you don't

256
00:15:24,440 --> 00:15:26,360
come clean about what you've done,

257
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:29,000
what's going to happen to you?

258
00:15:31,270 --> 00:15:32,720
Every parent

259
00:15:33,840 --> 00:15:36,080
wants to be there for their children

260
00:15:36,720 --> 00:15:38,240
and watch them grow up.

261
00:15:39,550 --> 00:15:40,910
I have a son too.

262
00:15:41,270 --> 00:15:43,150
But when he needed me the most,

263
00:15:44,840 --> 00:15:46,120
my colleagues and I

264
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:50,910
were out there protecting this city

265
00:15:51,510 --> 00:15:53,240
and keeping all of you safe.

266
00:15:53,960 --> 00:15:55,480
You have no idea how much I wish

267
00:15:56,240 --> 00:15:58,360
I could be there to watch him grow up.

268
00:16:02,510 --> 00:16:03,320
When a person

269
00:16:05,630 --> 00:16:06,600
loses all their money,

270
00:16:08,260 --> 00:16:09,370
they can always earn it back.

271
00:16:11,030 --> 00:16:12,510
But if they choose the wrong path,

272
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:17,240
there's no turning back.

273
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:19,750
We know your son's name is

274
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,000
Zhang Xiaoshan.

275
00:16:23,790 --> 00:16:25,080
That's a very nice name.

276
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:27,440
But Zhang Daxin,

277
00:16:28,870 --> 00:16:30,200
you are his father.

278
00:16:33,720 --> 00:16:35,600
More than that,
you're the mountain supporting him.

279
00:16:38,150 --> 00:16:40,320
If you collapse one day,

280
00:16:42,030 --> 00:16:43,790
this family will be gone.

281
00:16:46,630 --> 00:16:47,440
All right.

282
00:16:50,030 --> 00:16:50,870
Stop talking.

283
00:16:53,200 --> 00:16:55,000
I'll tell you everything I know.

284
00:17:02,550 --> 00:17:04,750
I didn't kill Liang Chao.

285
00:17:05,880 --> 00:17:07,110
I wanted to kill him,

286
00:17:07,110 --> 00:17:08,960
and I was looking for a chance.

287
00:17:09,310 --> 00:17:11,400
After the Urban Construction
scandal broke out,

288
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:13,510
a lot of people wanted to kill him.

289
00:17:14,960 --> 00:17:16,030
But he was too sly.

290
00:17:16,030 --> 00:17:17,240
He had already gone into hiding.

291
00:17:17,350 --> 00:17:18,440
Three months ago,

292
00:17:18,550 --> 00:17:20,000
I finally managed to track him down.

293
00:17:20,310 --> 00:17:21,480
I trailed him,

294
00:17:22,270 --> 00:17:23,310
waiting for a chance to strike.

295
00:17:23,920 --> 00:17:26,110
But who could have known that back then,

296
00:17:27,240 --> 00:17:28,310
something bizarre happened?

297
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:52,680
I didn't see clearly
who that person was,

298
00:17:52,880 --> 00:17:54,750
but Liang Chao surely knew him.

299
00:17:55,110 --> 00:17:56,790
I guess it was someone
who held a grudge against him.

300
00:17:56,960 --> 00:17:58,350
That's just how Liang Chao is,

301
00:17:58,680 --> 00:18:00,030
sucking up to Huo Qicheng,

302
00:18:00,030 --> 00:18:01,790
acting all high and mighty,

303
00:18:02,030 --> 00:18:03,030
and looking down on everyone.

304
00:18:03,830 --> 00:18:05,480
I tracked him all the way to a warehouse

305
00:18:05,480 --> 00:18:06,830
and waited patiently for a while.

306
00:18:07,480 --> 00:18:08,510
There was no one inside.

307
00:18:09,110 --> 00:18:11,440
I thought that was the perfect
opportunity to kill Liang Chao.

308
00:18:53,570 --> 00:18:58,090
♪The old walkie-talkie I treasure♪

309
00:19:01,160 --> 00:19:05,940
♪The birthday surprise
you gave me that year♪

310
00:19:08,650 --> 00:19:14,030
♪Its buttons worn
and weathered with time♪

311
00:19:14,560 --> 00:19:19,890
♪Still echoing your words,
"Be brave and keep moving on"♪

312
00:19:21,920 --> 00:19:29,880
♪The old train rolled over
our reluctance to part♪

313
00:19:30,510 --> 00:19:35,560
♪You waved goodbye
and faded into the night♪

314
00:19:37,600 --> 00:19:45,910
♪I used to think
we'd always have more time♪

315
00:19:45,910 --> 00:19:51,760
♪But that goodbye became the last♪

316
00:19:53,220 --> 00:20:01,340
♪I carry the warmth you left behind♪

317
00:20:02,030 --> 00:20:07,070
♪Making my way
through every door in life♪

318
00:20:08,850 --> 00:20:16,890
♪Whenever a train
whistle sounds at night♪

319
00:20:17,170 --> 00:20:24,440
♪I suddenly long to call out to you♪

320
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:29,050
♪Can you hear me?♪

321
00:20:29,060 --> 00:20:32,850
♪Can you hear me?♪

322
00:20:32,850 --> 00:20:40,310
♪Let the old receiver
carry the words I never said♪

323
00:20:40,310 --> 00:20:48,050
♪I've taken on
both your duty and your love♪

324
00:20:48,380 --> 00:20:53,990
♪This train has no return, and when I
look back, you're no longer waiting♪

325
00:20:55,870 --> 00:20:59,470
♪After all these years♪

326
00:21:01,980 --> 00:21:09,460
♪How I wish I could
talk to you just one more time♪

327
00:21:10,360 --> 00:21:11,660
♪And tell you♪

328
00:21:12,880 --> 00:21:16,150
♪I haven't let you down♪
